      "body": "## Background / motivation\n\n- Run an automatic Autobot review when a draft PR becomes ready for review.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `.github/autobot/review-config.yml` with:\n\n```yaml\nauto-review:\n  enabled: true\n  mode: comment\n  on: status_change\n  when: ready_for_review\n```\n\n## Details\n\n- `status_change` selects draft/readiness transitions; `when` filters the resulting PR state.\n- `mode: comment` publishes findings as a `COMMENT` review.\n- CI-Events reads the policy from the default branch, so it takes effect after merge.\n- Policy semantics: [CI-Events automatic-review documentation](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/CI-Events-Workflows/blob/2e210caf3db9fd6f7ab30d17282229ab5f86e681/apps/workflows/capability/review-github-pr/README.md#automatic-reviews).\n\n## Tested\n\n- `python3 ../validate_review_configs.py` (local validation harness) — loaded the CI-Events parser and selector from `2e210caf3db9fd6f7ab30d17282229ab5f86e681`; exact policy, comment mode, and all 22 action/state cases passed in all six target repositories.\n- `git diff --cached --check` — passed.\n- Model rollouts and training tests: N/A; only repository review configuration changes.\n",
